@startuml state-event-schedule
' Title: SM-03 Event schedule lifecycle (PlantUML version of state-event-schedule.mmd, keep both in sync)
' Source: enums/AreaEventScheduleStatus.java, service/AreaService.java (createSchedule, updateSchedule, cancelSchedule,
'   activateScheduleInTx, cleanupExpiredSessions, updateEventMode, finishScheduleOfSession),
'   scheduler/AreaEventModeScheduler.java · Generated from main @ e474968
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 65
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam stateStartColor #000000
skinparam stateEndColor #000000
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam stateBorderColor #475569
skinparam stateFontColor #0F172A
skinparam stateArrowColor #2563EB
hide empty description

title SM-03 Event Schedule Lifecycle

state SCHEDULED : booked, not started
state STARTED : event session open
state CANCELLED
state FAILED
state COMPLETED
state ENDED_EARLY

[*] --> SCHEDULED : Facility Manager creates schedule\n[active Confidential area, startAt > now,\nno overlap, budget ok]

SCHEDULED --> SCHEDULED : Facility Manager edits\n[same checks as create, note]
SCHEDULED --> CANCELLED : Facility Manager cancels\n[reason code and note]
SCHEDULED --> STARTED : System job every minute\n[startAt reached, endAt > now,\narea active and Confidential] / session opened
SCHEDULED --> FAILED : System job every minute\n[endAt already passed, or area inactive,\nor area no longer Confidential]

STARTED --> COMPLETED : System closes the session\n[plannedEnd reached]
STARTED --> ENDED_EARLY : Facility Manager stops the event\n(event mode DISABLE)

CANCELLED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]
COMPLETED --> [*]
ENDED_EARLY --> [*]

note right of STARTED
  An event opens only from a schedule.
  PATCH /event-mode accepts DISABLE only
  (ENABLE, ADJUST -> 400 ERR_AREA_058).
end note
@enduml
